{"repositoryId":1006013765,"availability":"available","full":"coldstone/agent-playground","name":"agent-playground","description":"A comprehensive playground for testing AI agents and models with support for multiple LLM providers","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":9,"forks":1,"created":"2025-06-21T09:45:23Z","updated":"2026-09-07T16:39:58Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://bot.hoho.tech","topics":[],"demo":"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:04.963Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:04.963Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:04.963Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T17:02:04.963Z","stars":9,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A development and debugging platform for AI agents. Agent Playground lets you build, run and inspect agents that reach the outside world through four kinds of tools — your own local HTTP tools, MCP servers over Streamable HTTP, Agent Skills written as SKILL.md, and a built-in Web Fetch that reads any public URL — against any of a dozen LLM providers. Everything runs in the browser: agents, tools, skills and conversations are stored locally in IndexedDB, and API keys never leave your machine.","New in 0.3.0: MCP servers (Streamable HTTP, dual-era) and Agent Skills (SKILL.md), both usable in every conversation. New in 0.3.1: built-in Web Fetch and Web Search — give the model a URL and it reads the page as clean Markdown, or let it search the web and follow up on what it finds."],"features":["Connect any Streamable HTTP MCP server and its tools become available to the model in every conversation.","Add by JSON: Paste a standard mcpServers config in the MCP Servers panel:","Add by form: Or fill in the URL and any static headers by hand — several servers can be pasted at once","Dual-era protocol: Speaks the stateless 2026-07-28 protocol and falls back to the legacy initialize handshake (2025-11-25 and earlier) automatically; the negotiated version is shown on the server card","Server-side proxy: All MCP traffic goes through Next.js API routes under /api/mcp, so there is no CORS to fight and your credentials only travel on the browser→server hop of your own instance"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/coldstone/agent-playground/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f3d6353cfb478cc67524a488c72e0c92aedfa536cfe0c8ba078bd7a3159a8fb2","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:05.098Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:05.098Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A development and debugging platform for AI agents. Agent Playground lets you build, run and inspect agents that reach the outside world through four kinds of tools — your own local HTTP tools, MCP servers over Streamable HTTP, Agent Skills written as SKILL.md, and a built-in Web Fetch that reads any public URL — against any of a dozen LLM providers. Everything runs in the browser: agents, tools, skills and conversations are stored locally in IndexedDB, and API keys never leave your machine.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/coldstone/agent-playground/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f3d6353cfb478cc67524a488c72e0c92aedfa536cfe0c8ba078bd7a3159a8fb2","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/coldstone/agent-playground/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:05.099Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-07T16:39:58Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/coldstone/agent-playground/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T17:02:05.101Z","hash":"f3d6353cfb478cc67524a488c72e0c92aedfa536cfe0c8ba078bd7a3159a8fb2","originalBytes":19350,"storedBytes":19350,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["tools","agent","tool","model","skill","web","mcp","server","fetch","api","bash","skills","start","built-in","chat","npm","run","search","page","panel","url","build","components","docker","only","call","card","development","http","ke